THE FOUR PRINCIPLES, applied in this order
  1 unit device      every member of a tie group is one device repeated
  2 maximal unit     as big as the PDK's widest model bin allows
  3 square device    one copy as tall as it is wide
  4 square array     the copies tile into a square block
  constraint         total width w*m preserved; residual bounded by --max-total-error 2.000% and reported below

PROCESS GEOMETRY (one copy = nf gate columns + nf+1 source/drain columns)
  source              glayout get_grule() on sky130_mapped
  sd_column           0.3300 um
  poly_extension      0.1300 um
  min finger width    1.000 um (floor on w_unit/nf)
  height = w_unit/nf + 2*poly_extension
  width  = nf*l + (nf+1)*sd_column

